Package: 1bit-systems
Version: 1.0.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6, libgomp1
Recommends: rocm-hip-runtime
Maintainer: admin@1bit.systems
Description: One binary, all backends — NPU + GPU + CPU inference engine
 1bit.systems is a pure C++23 inference engine for AMD Strix Halo
 (Ryzen AI Max+ 395): a single binary drives the XDNA 2 NPU, the
 Radeon 8060S GPU (ROCm HIP + Vulkan), and CPU fallback in one
 process. 40 models across 16 families in the native 1BP format,
 plus direct GGUF execution. Zero Python, zero Docker at runtime.
 .
 Requires a ROCm 7.15.0a-compatible HIP runtime (libhsa-runtime64)
 for GPU/NPU acceleration — see https://1bit.systems for install
 instructions. CPU-only operation works without it.
 .
 Includes: 1bit (CLI), onebit/onebitd (agent + daemon), zaya_server
 (HIP inference + OpenAI-compatible API), unified_router.
